      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.85,
      "end_seconds": 20.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "good that'll be useful pull up a chair"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 21.73,
      "end_seconds": 24.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "we came because of tiredness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.05,
      "end_seconds": 28.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "how many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.04,
      "end_seconds": 42.47,
      "duration_seconds": 12.43,
      "text": "okay, so it's been going on for about three months i've also had night sweats, for two months as for night sweats, it feels mild to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.02,
      "end_seconds": 48.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "have you had tiredness before or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.43,
      "end_seconds": 58.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "oh, yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.09,
      "end_seconds": 62.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.54,
      "end_seconds": 71.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "nearly done with the readings.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.75,
      "end_seconds": 94.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "okay: BP is 117 over 70 temperature 39.0 pulse 107."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.67,
      "end_seconds": 97.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is that that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.74,
      "end_seconds": 106.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination have you had any chest pain, weight loss or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.24,
      "end_seconds": 115.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "No chest pain, weight loss or cough, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.35,
      "end_seconds": 120.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.37,
      "end_seconds": 123.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "no, my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.3,
      "end_seconds": 132.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.14,
      "end_seconds": 140.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.16,
      "end_seconds": 147.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.89,
      "end_seconds": 152.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.45,
      "end_seconds": 157.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Okay, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.5,
      "end_seconds": 166.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Anxiety, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.93,
      "end_seconds": 185.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.0,
      "end_seconds": 188.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.49,
      "end_seconds": 191.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.0,
      "end_seconds": 197.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.6,
      "end_seconds": 200.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.54,
      "end_seconds": 204.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.79,
      "end_seconds": 223.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.7,
      "end_seconds": 229.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 231.94,
      "end_seconds": 241.36,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "Yeah, it's meant to be once a day, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.89,
      "end_seconds": 258.82,
      "duration_seconds": 15.93,
      "text": "from what you've told me, the most likely explanation is possible infective endocarditis that's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more a viral illness is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.38,
      "end_seconds": 260.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.74,
      "end_seconds": 269.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "I can't promise yet but most people with possible infective endocarditis do well once it's treated properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.27,
      "end_seconds": 292.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Blood tests is what I'd like next, for prolonged fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.81,
      "end_seconds": 296.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.03,
      "end_seconds": 321.78,
      "duration_seconds": 23.75,
      "text": "let's get an echocardiogram, for new murmur. Blood cultures is what I'd like next, for possible endocarditis you need admission today for Blood cultures and a heart scan please don't wait if the symptoms get worse that's when to be seen urgently i'd like to see you again straight away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.63,
      "end_seconds": 326.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "actually, I can manage that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.71,
      "end_seconds": 330.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "alright, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.25,
      "end_seconds": 334.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "alright thanks take care"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.98,
      "end_seconds": 336.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
